<Learn
  title="India Atlas — Learn · The base year: the ruler's zero mark"
  description="Learn № 16 — why statistics carry a year in their name (CPI base 2012=100, GDP base 2011–12), what a base revision changes and what it cannot, and why an old base drifts from how India actually lives."
  slug="base-year"
  kicker="Learn № 16 — Reading numbers · The base year"
  h1="2012 = 100 is a ruler's <i>zero mark.</i>"
  lede="Every Indian statistic carries a year in its name, and that year does two quiet jobs: it sets the zero against which everything is measured, and it freezes the weights that decide what counts. This page is about what changes when the year is moved, and what can never change."
  meta={[
